00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.710
Now, this is the second biggest
bank failure in US history.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.941
You're talking about a bank
that had nearly 200 billion

00:01:37.941 --> 00:01:41.340
in deposits just about a quarter ago,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:42.540
a little over a quarter ago

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:45.120
at the end of 2022 that has been seized.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:46.710
It was seized by the FDIC,

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:48.630
the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation,

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.940
and sold to JP Morgan Chase.

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.660
JPM assuming all of First
Republic's 92 billion dollars

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:56.310
remaining in deposits.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:57.930
Also buying most of the bank's assets

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.780
including 173 billion dollars in loans,

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.420
30 billion dollars in security.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.844
The FDIC hit, that's
the taxpayer is gonna be

00:02:06.844 --> 00:02:08.520
$13 billion dollars
from its insurance fund.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:11.760
The FDIC has insurance fund
for just these sorts of things.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.060
JP Morgan also said it will
receive 50 billion dollars

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.670
in financing from FDIC.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.370
This is the second largest
failure after if y'all remember

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.548
Washington Mutual back in 2008

00:02:22.548 --> 00:02:23.730
that was the largest.

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:24.563
This is bigger

00:02:24.563 --> 00:02:26.400
than Silicon Valley Bank,
bigger than Signature.

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.513
This was the Nation's 14th largest bank.

00:02:29.513 --> 00:02:31.016
This is big news.

00:02:31.016 --> 00:02:32.670
Interesting to note,

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:35.640
JP Morgan also is the bank that
took over Washington Mutual.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.270
So, now JP Morgan is the
buyer or the company taking

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:43.110
over the number one and number
two largest bank failures

00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.850
in the history of the US.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:47.220
So, really quickly, how did we get here?

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:50.040
Well, listen, most recently you
guys have seen what happened

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.960
with Silicon Valley Bank, Signature Bank,

00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.450
just this rush of deposits out the door

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.730
while investors found
out First Republic lost

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:00.060
about a hundred billion
dollars in deposits

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.300
in a March run on the bank
following its earnings reports

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.920
that just came out last week.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.270
Now, the bank stock lost almost
50% of its value in one day.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.610
That was just investors
saying, we have no confidence

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.350
that after this a hundred billion dollars

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:16.260
in deposits went out the door,
this bank can still hold up.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.000
The bank only had taken

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.940
on about 30 billion dollars
in deposits from the Big Five.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:24.270
That's US Bank, Wells Fargo, JP Morgan

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.310
which now owns the bank, Citigroup

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.470
and those guys, those big names.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.060
But they were unable to sell

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.280
or put a deal together before
they reported earnings.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:35.404
And once they reported that a
hundred-billion-dollar loss,

00:03:35.404 --> 00:03:38.460
man, the wolves were in
the stock, was sold out.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.500
And this was a huge, huge loss.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.360
You had a collection
of uninsured deposits.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.030
Now, if you've seen
the run on these banks,

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.330
what we saw and what we
have seen is just a run

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.849
on the banks from the biggest

00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:53.370
or from the banks with the
most uninsured deposits.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.680
Uninsured deposits are basically deposits

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:57.720
that are over $250,000.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.720
The FDIC says, we're not gonna
ensure that you take the risk

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.820
if you put money in a bank
that's over that amount.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.200
Silicon Valley Bank had 97% of
its deposits were uninsured.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.480
Signature Bank, 90% of its deposits.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:11.280
First Republic, 68%.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.360
So, what comes next?

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.700
Well, the next largest
bank or the next bank

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:17.273
with the largest share of deposits,

00:04:17.273 --> 00:04:18.960
uninsured EastWest Bank 67%,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.400
Comerica with 64%, Western Alliance 55%,

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:28.019
Pack West 52, Zion's Bank
51, KeyCorp 47% are KeyBank.

00:04:28.019 --> 00:04:31.950
So listen, all those are
are stocks to watch out for.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:32.783
Keep your eye.

