00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.100
That's because there's
worry about recession.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:05.933
There's worry.

00:10:05.933 --> 00:10:07.110
Oh, maybe these things won't get paid.

00:10:07.110 --> 00:10:08.700
But there's also worry

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:11.190
that the Federal Reserve is
going to start cutting rates.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:13.290
They're gonna keep rates
high in the interim,

00:10:13.290 --> 00:10:15.420
in the short term, and then start cutting.

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.460
And that's a lot of what you're
seeing in that yield curve.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.410
So, that what you're seeing right there

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:21.750
that chart illustrating expectations

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:24.180
for what the Federal
Reserve is going to do next.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.980
Folks expect that they'll keep rates high

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.380
