00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:32.400
And that we're likely
headed into a recession,

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:33.780
which is going to force the Fed

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:35.041
to lower rates significantly.

00:10:35.041 --> 00:10:38.340
And that's why you're seeing
those lower rates longer term.

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.380
So, what the Fed does

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:42.360
at its next meaning is
all the way priced in.

00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:44.160
We have also seen a significant loosening

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:46.710
of financial conditions,
meaning stock prices higher.

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:49.077
The S&amp;P is of about 8.6% year to date.

00:10:49.077 --> 00:10:52.350
The Nasdaq of about 16% year to date

